<title>NORWAY: POLL - UBN H1 profits seen higher.</title>
<headline>POLL - UBN H1 profits seen higher.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Bank of Norway (UBN), Norway's largest  savings bank, is expected to post a first-half 1997 pre-tax operating  profit of nearly 700 million crowns, according to six analysts polled  by Reuters.</p>
<p>The corresponding 1996 profit was 761 million crowns.</p>
<p>Five analysts had a buy recommendation on the share, known as a primary  capital certificate, and one said hold.</p>
<p>UBN, Norway's third largest bank and known locally as Sparebanken  NOR, will present the figures on August 7.</p>
<p>				   (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>				    Expectations H1 1997</p>
<p>				    Average    Low     High     H1 1996</p>
<p> Net interest income	   1,230    1,213   1,242     1,241</p>
<p> Non-interest oper. income     937	930     951	 778</p>
<p> Operating costs		 1,440    1,417   1,454     1,353</p>
<p> Oper. profit before losses    726	701     749	 666</p>
<p> Pre-tax operating profit	697	676     720	 761</p>
<p> Net profit			  513	493     529	 559</p>
<p> EPS (crowns)		     13.59    13.24  14.30</p>
<p> EPS 1997			   26.79    26.33  27.10</p>
<p> EPS 1998			   26.96    24.40  29.71</p>
<p> Dividend 1997		    15.00    15.00  15.00</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, Alf Asklund +47 22 93 69 71</p>
